NAME
       telinit - change the run level (old style; switches systemd targets)

SYNOPSIS
       telinit RUNLEVEL

DESCRIPTION
       Before systemd, Linux systems had numbered run levels. telinit (and
       init N) still accepts those numbers on RHEL 9 and switches to the
       matching systemd target:

           0      poweroff.target (switch off)
           1, s   rescue.target (single user)
           2,3,4  multi-user.target (text console, network)
           5      graphical.target (graphical login)
           6      reboot.target (restart)

       New work should use systemctl isolate TARGET, systemctl reboot or
       systemctl poweroff directly.

EXAMPLES
           telinit 3

SEE ALSO
       systemctl(1), runlevel(8), init(1)
